      "mergeID": "5b9f96db322a3f7a49267647",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Allow (model) Muting of avatars that are over a certain distance away, that way if you are in a full level with everyone in your friends list you can still get some performance gain.\n\nIt's like a forced LOD for characters, preferably the switch radius could be customised (like between 2 and 15 meters)\n\nNow you can only mute people who are not in your friends list, but lately there are a lot of tight communities forming where everyone knows everyone so that method goes out the window.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Distance based Avatar (model) Muting",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a87b2473219f25c9bb0a7d7",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "This would be amazing for VRChat's dance communities! The ability to hang out with avatars nearby while distant avatars are disabled/blocked would help immensely with performance. If this is implemented, as a suggestion it would be nice to have a mode for blocking all avatars, even friends, or for blocking non-friends like the current block avatars by default function. The configurable radius is a must for partying because even with this feature it wouldn't help on a tightly packed dance floor if a static default radius was too large.\n\nAlso, to avoid lag spikes from quickly toggling avatars on and off as they ride the threshold, the mute radius should be larger than the enable avatar radius, such that you have to step closer to see the avatar but it takes more distance to get it to re-mute.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
