      "value": "Detailed Ideas:\neg1 (Based on Trusted Level):\nRender Players if \n{\nVisitors.distance<1unit;\nNewUser.distance<2units;\nUser.distance<3units;\nKnown.distance<5units;\nTrusted.distance<10units;\nFreinds=Always\n}\nThe range can be adjusted in the settings. \neg2 (Based on Safety Levels): \nif (0unit<Player.distance<1unit){use Safety.None on them} \nelseif (1unit<Player.distance<5units){use Safety.Normal on them} \nelse {use Safety.Maximum on them}\neg3 (Based on Avatar/Player features)\nRenderOrPlayIf\n{\n(Voice,Player.distance<16units),\n(Avatar,Player.distance<12units),\n(User Icon,Player.distance<8units),\n(Audio,Player.distance<2units),\n(Lights & Particles,Player.distance<1unit),\n(Shaders,Player.distance<1unit),are \n(Custom Animations,Player.distance<1unit)\n}\neg4 (Allow some special players to be rendered not using the Range rule)\nlet players choose a specific player, say a celebrity, and always render the celebrity or not render him/her. \nIt is similar to \"Show Avatar / Hide Avatar / Use Safety Settings\", \nit could be something like \n\"Show Avatar / Hide Avatar / Use Safety Settings (if this update is available, I prefer to call this \"Stationary Safety Settings\") / Use Range Safety Settings\"\neg5 (for Instance Maintainance)\n> the Instance Master can set if the instance could be an \"Event Instance\", where only Medium or better avatars are allowed, or maybe Poor or Better (can be set by the Instance Master )\n> before any player logs in to the instance, a screen will show them that the instance they are joining is an \"Event Instance\", so they would have to change their avatars.\n> while in an Event Instance, when launching the Launch Pad / Quick Menu, just like we have red beams for Cameras,  a beam would be given to Players who are using an avatar which is below the required level. So the \"authority\" can \"hunt\" them down and ask them to change their avatars or cruelly kick them.\n> Here we have a new Networking Role : Authority : a player who can kick/Ban annoying players immediately but not the Instance Master. an \"Authority\" can be selected by the Instance Master (or can be multiple of them)\nUsers can choose those who are outside the range can be\n> not rendered\n> rendered as the default stick man\n> rendered as their fallback avatar\nI know... that's a lot OwO",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
