  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-17T04:40:39.427Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A slider that lets you change how close a person must be for their character to render would be a welcome addition. This would allow you to interact with those close to you, and not have distance players in large groups from causing you frame lag. Players would still render as the \"loading\" model that you see when you log into a world before models load, when at a distance, so you could still see the presence of players. No animations would load for those players far away either, which I feel would reduce server lag, since a players animations, or every action would not have to be sent to all players any longer. \n- Would default to max distance (so as is).\n- Would sometimes be able to prevent those models and animatons that blanket a whole world with light and such.\n- Be useful for streamers.",
